{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144390-questions-on-spirits","id":1144390,"title":"Questions on Spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-27T07:10:27-07:00","id":1144390,"title":"Questions on Spirits","content":"As a primarily vampire play, I don't know the rules in regards to how a number of things for the Werewolf cosmology work, but I was thinking about folding a few in on a game I'm in. Primarily through the use of Thaumaturgy's Path of Spirit Manipulation.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to the actual questions I was curious on.<br /> - How would a typical spirit view a vampire?<br /> - How would a bane specifically view one?<br /> - Can you make a fetish with a Bane?<br /> - Are spirits in general and Banes receptive to deals with non-Fera if they contact them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T07:54:27-07:00","id":1144411,"title":"","content":"1/)Depends on the spirit. A Gaian spirit would detest a vampire as an unnatural affront to the Earthmother. <br /> 2/)Perhaps a bit friendlier; vampires <i>do</i> have infernalists, after all, meaning peaceful interaction between Banes and Cainites can and does happen.<br /> 3/)Yes. Black Spiral Dancers do this all the time. Gaian Garou, however, view Bane fetishes as unholy and worthy only of cleansing and/or destruction.<br /> 4/)Depends on the spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T08:34:41-07:00","id":1144429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1/)Depends on the spirit. A Gaian spirit would detest a vampire as an unnatural affront to the Earthmother. </div> </div> </div>I want to higlight this. While there are implications here and there that spirits don't like vampires, I think it's rather wrong to think all spirits do so.<br /> <br /> In particular, I don't remember astral spirits in general hating vampires. Tremere come from Hermetic mages. Hermetic mages in Mage make deals with the Astral, &quot;the high umbra&quot;. It would make sense for Tremere to work and make deals with these spirits too (well, at least those with an evil bent). There are elementals (and demons too) in the Astral Umbra, and these are the spirits that Tremere use to summon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T17:18:54-07:00","id":1144566,"title":"","content":"This is how I view it.<br /> <br /> 1) Gaian spirits would view the vampire as unnatural and not want to have anything to do with them. Some of those spirits might be particularly hostile. Things like &quot;Astral Spirits&quot; aren't part of the Gaian Penumbra that Garou are involved in. Instead, they'd be entities of the Astral Plane which vampires with Astral Projection routinely encounter as well as &quot;spirits&quot; that appear to be angelic or demonic.<br /> 2) Bane spirits are said to often follow a vampire around to relish in the pain and suffering they produce to their victims. So they'd be slightly favorable in general especially to the lower Humanity vampires who do more harm.<br /> 3) Yes. Black Spiral Dancers and even some Fomori use Wyrm fetishes.<br /> 4) Perhaps. They would not agree to become bound into Fetishes and the like (vampires don't have a Pact with spirits and wouldn't be trusted to fulfill promises made), but they would be willing to make Faustian deals so the vampire falls even further into corruption. Such dealings should be treated similarly as you would with Infernalism. In other words, in the end the vampire should always get the shaft somehow if they agree to a deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T17:48:51-07:00","id":1144574,"title":"","content":"Actually, Tremere <i>can</i> make fetishes. Rites of Blood for V20 has a Path power that does it. <i>However</i>, these fetishes are incredibly simplistic and lack the sheer flexibility of fetishes made by werecreatures or mages, merely being dice-adding items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T18:05:32-07:00","id":1144582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144390-questions-on-spirits?p=1144574#post1144574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Tremere <i>can</i> make fetishes. Rites of Blood for V20 has a Path power that does it. <i>However</i>, these fetishes are incredibly simplistic and lack the sheer flexibility of fetishes made by werecreatures or mages, merely being dice-adding items.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that those aren't Fetishes in the same respect that Werewolf uses the term. They're nothing alike except for the term used.<br /> <br /> Although that is probably because Vampire doesn't want to involve the full scope of Fetishes in WtA in one level of a semi-obscure path of blood magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T05:18:18-07:00","id":1144709,"title":"","content":"Cool answers! Couple followups.<br /> - What qualifies as an astral spirit? I know the astral plane and umbra are poorly seperated in Vampire, but what goes on in the High Umbra?<br /> - Do bane fetishes work differently than a normal fetish or just in regards to the type of bane?<br /> - As Demigod Beast somewhat noted, I was hoping to use Spirit Manipulation, but possibly fold back to Revised version in regards to making actual fetishes instead of the neutered version. What sort of deals would a bane spirit theoretically want?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T12:11:26-07:00","id":1144880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144390-questions-on-spirits?p=1144709#post1144709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool answers! Couple followups.<br /> - What qualifies as an astral spirit? I know the astral plane and umbra are poorly seperated in Vampire, but what goes on in the High Umbra?<br /> - Do bane fetishes work differently than a normal fetish or just in regards to the type of bane?<br /> - As Demigod Beast somewhat noted, I was hoping to use Spirit Manipulation, but possibly fold back to Revised version in regards to making actual fetishes instead of the neutered version. What sort of deals would a bane spirit theoretically want?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The higher umbra is something like a strange world of ideas and concepts. The heavens and hells of legens and religions can be found here and there are realms like the astral reaches, a kind of world on the clouds, where you can encounter several angel-like spirits and others.<br /> <br /> For bane fetishes, I'd personaly put a twist on them. They might be slightly more powerfull but corrupt the user over time. (Edit: That's to say, have negative impacts like lowering the SG to frenzy or encourage sins of humanity. Maybe requiring a daily bath in human blood to work (the item, not the vampire <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ))<br /> <br /> As for what a bane would want... well, there are tons of possibilities. Banes are spirits of corruption, working either for the urge wyrms (think along the lines of the seven biblical sins, abrahamic lore is always a good fit for Vampire) or corruption in general. A bane of greed could want it's new home to be made of only the finest gold, maybe even stolen from the tomb of a long dead king or whatever. But not the material would be what really matters for the bane, but the act of stealing, unearthing ancient treasures and defiling graves and such. For a bane everything goes, as long as it spreads, furthers and expands corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","user":"TheVarulfen","date":". 09-28-2017, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T13:49:15-07:00","id":1144924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheValufren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The higher umbra is something like a strange world of ideas and concepts. The heavens and hells of legens and religions can be found here and there are realms like the astral reaches, a kind of world on the clouds, where you can encounter several angel-like spirits and others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. There's also the elemental courts where &quot;conceptual&quot; elementals reside, spirits of mathematical concepts, spirits of social concepts like leadership, spirits that represent epochs and such. It's a varied place, like all the Umbra.<br /> <br /> All human pantheons have an astral representation where spirits of gods and godesses reside. For instance, if a Tremere wants to summon Zeus or the Muses, you can get that from the astral umbra because these beings are the representation of very important concepts and beliefs. If the spirit would be willing to make a deal depends on their nature (on the concept the spirit represents).<br /> There may be (and surely are) spirits similar to human gods in the middle umbra, but then you would have to be careful to not summon a Gaian spirit. The Patriarch, a Weaver Incarna, and Grandfather Thunder, the Garou Totem, may both have a zeus-like avatar, but these come with their patron's baggages<br /> <br /> I also whant ot ask: What about the Weaver?. Vampires are kinda &quot;of the wyrm&quot;, but also kinda static. May Weaver aligned spirits be willing to talk or deal with a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T01:48:09-07:00","id":1145134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144390-questions-on-spirits?p=1144924#post1144924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also whant ot ask: What about the Weaver?. Vampires are kinda &quot;of the wyrm&quot;, but also kinda static. May Weaver aligned spirits be willing to talk or deal with a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question. I feel vampires are kind of an odd thing to the Weaver or weaver spirits. The way it is represented in the Book of the Weaver she is not really concerned with this type of supernatural or supernaturals in general. Aside from glasswalker garou and the technocracy there is no direct correlation to between her and supernaturals. Rather, the weaver focuses on human kind. Vampires are static but the Weaver is progress (as in: progress in only one, very controlled, direction).<br /> Personally I'd focus on banes and wraiths for a vampire game, especially if I as a ST don't know much about the other ephermic stuff. They fit the theme of Vampire perfectly and are not as complicated or weird as weaver and wyld spirits.<br /> <br /> Stasis is of course interesting for Vampire as it represents one aspect of the vampire nature. The blood sucking Ananasi are mostly weaver related (well Ananasa related really) and might present some interesting riddle to solve for the PCs, but real spirits are kind of... off. Weaver spirits also tend to be tech spirits and entities that represent scientific methods or advancement. It seems a bit untypical for a vampire to assume he could call a spirit of laptops or influence traffic by calling out to an entity of the traffic lights in the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T13:20:08-07:00","id":1145339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144390-questions-on-spirits#post1144390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- How would a typical spirit view a vampire?<br /> - How would a bane specifically view one?<br /> - Can you make a fetish with a Bane?<br /> - Are spirits in general and Banes receptive to deals with non-Fera if they contact them?<br /> <br /> - What qualifies as an astral spirit? I know the astral plane and umbra are poorly seperated in Vampire, but what goes on in the High Umbra?<br /> - Do bane fetishes work differently than a normal fetish or just in regards to the type of bane?<br /> - As Demigod Beast somewhat noted, I was hoping to use Spirit Manipulation, but possibly fold back to Revised version in regards to making actual fetishes instead of the neutered version. What sort of deals would a bane spirit theoretically want?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Depends on the spirit. Gaia-aligned won't like them, Weaver and Wyrm spirits are probably going to ignore them unless disturbed. Elementals are, usually, quite oblivious to this kind of faction play and self-absorbed in their own elemental-aligned goals. There is, however, very little contact between spirits and vampires, perhaps a couple of thaumaturgical paths allow to interact with them.<br /> <br /> 2) Banes are not allies of the vampires and there's no guarantee they're even going to share a goal. Banes are interested in corruption, destruction, domination and feeding, pursuing those goals in a way suitable to their nature: a Greed bane will be attracted by greedy people, feed from them (=absorbing quintessence/life energy and leaving them weak or even hurt), instigate greed in the people around them and sometimes, in the worst cases, possess them and alter their bodies (creating a fomori).<br /> <br /> A Vampire may persuade a Bane to help, if summoned or approached by someone competent enough to offer them an appropriate chiminage (=payment) for whatever they're asking, or may find himself fighting it if he's messing with the Bane's hunting spot. Vampires can be even possessed by banes, but only a few spirits will consider their bodies as an appropriate host (the book of wyrm suggests banes of blood and of madness) and only the strongest ones can manage it.<br /> <br /> 4) Depends by a hella lot of factors. Firstly, how the spirit views the summoner (vampire, werewolf, human, etc). Secondly, what the spirit wants that the summoner can offer. Thirdly, the summoner's knowledge of the spirit world (proper etiquette, general Umbra politics, making an adequate offer, etc). Fourth, the sheer difference in powers: if the summoner, through appropriate rituals and disciplines, is able to bind a spirit by strength he doesn't even need to make a bargain - like with spirit manipulation 3.<br /> <br /> Some mages are quite competent in summoning, binding and dealing with spirits though, so it's not like an activity reserved to shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> 5) many already answered this, so I'm only adding that High Umbra is mostly used in Mage chronicles rather than WtA, you might want to check MtA material.<br /> <br /> 6) No, they're normal fetishes. Different spirits will require different payments and offer different powers.<br /> <br /> 7) What neutered version? The spirit hostility is there only because the power assume to bind it against its will, but if you let the vampire find an agreement the spirit may enter the fetish willingly without even a willpower roll. About the chiminage: it's completely dependent by the type and power of the bane, not to mention what you ask from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 09-30-2017, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T13:26:09-07:00","id":1145341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144390-questions-on-spirits?p=1145339#post1145339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7) What neutered version? The spirit hostility is there only because the power assume to bind it against its will, but if you let the vampire find an agreement the spirit may enter the fetish willingly without even a willpower roll. About the chiminage: it's completely dependent by the type and power of the bane, not to mention what you ask from it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I appreciate all the answers! Quite in-depth. In revised Spirit Manipulation would allow once to make straight WtA type fetishes. V20 you just make fetishes that gives a +1-5 bonus to certain actions the fetish is helpful in. Which I find a lot less interesting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T16:53:35-07:00","id":1145387,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine that a lot of astral spirits would still not like vampires, because &quot;astral spirit&quot; is as broad as &quot;middle umbral spirit&quot;. If an astral spirit involves the concept of illumination, truth, or freedom, it's going to try to cut their cord and burn their astral self into a cloud of conceptual ashes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144390-questions-on-spirits?p=1144924#post1144924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. There's also the elemental courts where &quot;conceptual&quot; elementals reside, spirits of mathematical concepts, spirits of social concepts like leadership, spirits that represent epochs and such. It's a varied place, like all the Umbra.<br /> <br /> All human pantheons have an astral representation where spirits of gods and godesses reside. For instance, if a Tremere wants to summon Zeus or the Muses, you can get that from the astral umbra because these beings are the representation of very important concepts and beliefs. If the spirit would be willing to make a deal depends on their nature (on the concept the spirit represents).<br /> There may be (and surely are) spirits similar to human gods in the middle umbra, but then you would have to be careful to not summon a Gaian spirit. The Patriarch, a Weaver Incarna, and Grandfather Thunder, the Garou Totem, may both have a zeus-like avatar, but these come with their patron's baggages</div> </div> </div> </div>Grandfather Thunder could manifest as a bearded old man, but he'd probably be keener to appear as a brooding, dark presence that can't be pinned down too much, with lots of shadows. Zarok, Incarna of Jupiter, might be more inclined to appear as a bearded old man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also whant ot ask: What about the Weaver?. Vampires are kinda &quot;of the wyrm&quot;, but also kinda static. May Weaver aligned spirits be willing to talk or deal with a vampire? </div> </div> </div>The older a vampire is, the more it registers to Sense Weaver (as in, a reduction of difficulty per milestone of time). So if a vampiric occultist is quite old, weaver-spirits might be more favorably inclined to listen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T17:03:04-07:00","id":1145388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144390-questions-on-spirits?p=1145341#post1145341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I appreciate all the answers! Quite in-depth. In revised Spirit Manipulation would allow once to make straight WtA type fetishes. V20 you just make fetishes that gives a +1-5 bonus to certain actions the fetish is helpful in. Which I find a lot less interesting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's supposed to be. If it allowed the Vampire to make real Fetishes (WtA), it would make that level (and Path) far too powerful in comparison to other Paths/Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idper